abf: register the error counters of abf-input-ip6

abf_input_inline counts ABF_ERROR_MATCHED and ABF_ERROR_MISSED on the
node of the address family it runs for, but abf-input-ip6 was registered
with .n_errors = 0. Its error heap index stays 0, so the counts land on
global error indices 1 and 2, which belong to whatever node comes first
in the error heap. On the 26.06 builds here that is wg4-output-tun-handoff: every
IPv6 packet that misses ABF showed up as a WireGuard "congestion drop".
Register the same error strings as abf-input-ip4.

--- a/src/plugins/abf/abf_itf_attach.c
+++ b/src/plugins/abf/abf_itf_attach.c
@@ -658,7 +658,8 @@
   .vector_size = sizeof (u32),
   .format_trace = format_abf_input_trace,
   .type = VLIB_NODE_TYPE_INTERNAL,
-  .n_errors = 0,
+  .n_errors = ABF_N_ERROR,
+  .error_strings = abf_error_strings,
   .n_next_nodes = ABF_N_NEXT,
 
   .next_nodes =
